#
# How to cite this project, in the Citation File Format 1.2.0
# (https://citation-file-format.github.io/). It describes the release named in
# version and date-released, and is updated with each release. The original
# hMailServer, by Martin Knafve, is cited as the work this one is a fork of.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file. It is
  Progressive Robot's fork of hMailServer; the original hMailServer is cited in its
  references.
type: software
title: hMailServer
abstract: >-
  Progressive Robot's fork of hMailServer, not the original hMailServer by Martin
  Knafve, which is developed separately. hMailServer is a free, open-source mail
  server: SMTP, IMAP and POP3, with anti-spam and anti-virus filtering, DKIM, DMARC,
  ARC, MTA-STS and DANE, a webmail client, a browser administration console and a
  REST API, on Windows and, from the fork's 6.3.0, on Linux. Progressive Robot Ltd
  forked it in 2026, and the fork's releases begin at 6.0.0, of 12 June 2026.
authors:
  - given-names: Christopher
    family-names: Holloway
    affiliation: Progressive Robot Ltd
  - name: Progressive Robot Ltd
    website: https://www.progressiverobot.com
version: 6.3.7
date-released: 2026-10-17
license: AGPL-3.0-or-later
repository-code: https://gitlab.com/hmailserver/hmailserver
url: https://gitlab.com/hmailserver/hmailserver
keywords:
  - mail server
  - email
  - SMTP
  - IMAP
  - POP3
  - DKIM
  - DMARC
  - webmail
references:
  - type: software
    title: hMailServer
    abstract: >-
